    "problem_statement": "Hook manager flush not writing newlines properly\n\n#### Description\n\nThe hook manager's flush functionality is not working correctly. When `flush_buffers()` is called, it should write a newline to properly separate output, but it appears to be writing empty strings instead.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom alive_progress.core.hook_manager import hook\nfrom alive_progress.core.hook_manager import install_hook\n\nhook_manager = hook('')\nwith install_hook(hook_manager):\n    print('ok', end='')\n    # At this point, output should be buffered\n    hook_manager.flush_buffers()\n    # Expected: 'ok\\n' should be written to stdout\n    # Actual: Nothing or empty string is written\n```\n\nThe issue seems to affect the buffering mechanism where flushed content doesn't get the expected newline termination."
  }
